request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist, search, movie-detail, app  (Field rename only: watchlist items (Movie and WatchItem) now carry `seen: boolean` instead of `watched: boolean`. movie redefines the types; watchlist-store updates every read/write of the field (add, toggleWatched, watchedCount, persistence); watchlist updates logic and template bindings; search, movie-detail and app get audit-only steps in case they reference the field. Exported names such as toggleWatched and watchedCount are method/signal names, not the data field, and stay unchanged. Acceptance tests pin the new field on the types and on store behavior.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected search=ok movie-detail=ok app=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (Round 1 is red only because of the watchlist unit: its template still references the old `watched` field (TS2339 x3) and its existing spec asserts `store.items()[0].watched`. The watchlist owner already produced the correct fix but it was auto-rejected solely for modifying that existing test. That modification is exactly what this rename requires (the field is now `seen`), so I approve it and re-instruct only the watchlist unit. All other units are green or unaffected.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The rename from `watched` to `seen` is complete: tsc is clean and all 32 tests pass, including the acceptance tests pinning the new `seen` field on Movie, WatchItem, and the store's persisted/toggled state. The watchlist owner's test modification (asserting `seen` instead of `watched`) was part of the requested rename and is approved.)

